## Key Learnings

1. Apache Pekko publishes the restart-stash overflow as Dropped with no sender and reason "Stash is full in [RestartSupervisor]" (Supervision.scala:120-124, SupervisionSpec.scala:908).
2. Pekko's typed ask against a terminated or missing actor fails with a TimeoutException whose message says "had already been terminated" (AskPattern.scala:147-150, AskSpec.scala:71 and :109).
3. In Pekko Props the "first" occurrence found from the head is the most recently added setting, and no public API builds two ActorTags nodes (Props.scala:35-40, PropsAdapter.scala:53).
4. SupervisionSpec.scala:1671 is only a comment, so no Pekko spec asserts that Resume does not rerun setup; the nesting tests at :163 and :208 run on BehaviorTestKit.
5. Pekko MDC from withMdc is thread-local and reaches every SLF4J logger of the turn, including logMessages entries (LogMessagesSpec.scala:95-137), which differs from the kit-logger With mapping of ADR 0033 D11.
